{"name":"Saxony Blue","hex":"#216b88","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saxony","blocks":[{"text":"Saxony, officially the Free State of Saxony, is a landlocked state of Germany, bordering the states of Brandenburg, Saxony-Anhalt, Thuringia, and Bavaria, as well as the countries of the Czech Republic and Poland. Its capital is Dresden, and its largest city is Leipzig. Saxony is the tenth largest of Germany's sixteen states, with an area of 18,450 square kilometres (7,124 sq mi), and the seventh most populous, with more than 4 million inhabitants. Together with Saxony-Anhalt and Thuringia, Saxony is one of the three states commonly associated with Central Germany."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Flag_of_Saxony.svg/330px-Flag_of_Saxony.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saxony"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heinrich_der_L%C3%B6we_und_Mathilde_von_England.jpg/500px-Heinrich_der_L%C3%B6we_und_Mathilde_von_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heinrich_der_L%C3%B6we_und_Mathilde_von_England.jpg/1280px-Heinrich_der_L%C3%B6we_und_Mathilde_von_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heinrich_der_L%C3%B6we_und_Mathilde_von_England.jpg/500px-Heinrich_der_L%C3%B6we_und_Mathilde_von_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Henry the Lion (with his wife Matilda of England, Duchess of Saxony) being crowned as the Duke of Saxony","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeinrich_der_L%C3%B6we_und_Mathilde_von_England.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Albrechtsburg01.jpg/500px-Albrechtsburg01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Albrechtsburg01.jpg/500px-Albrechtsburg01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Meissen, with Albrechtsburg and Cathedral","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbrechtsburg01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Saxony_after_the_Capitulation_of_Wittenberg_%281547%29_-_DE.png/500px-Saxony_after_the_Capitulation_of_Wittenberg_%281547%29_-_DE.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content